Let me massage it.

268
00:14:19,922 --> 00:14:22,091
-No, the right leg.
-The other one.

269
00:14:22,592 --> 00:14:24,010
Here? Down below?

270
00:14:24,093 --> 00:14:25,178
-Now, the left.
-The left.

271
00:14:25,678 --> 00:14:27,597
-[Kyungjin] Down below?
-[Isoo] Yeah, down below.

272
00:14:27,680 --> 00:14:28,681
[inhales sharply]

273
00:14:29,265 --> 00:14:30,975
[Jaeeun] Do you have a clear shot?

274
00:14:31,058 --> 00:14:32,727
Yes, a really clear shot.

275
00:14:33,227 --> 00:14:35,104
Shouldn't we be evacuating?

276
00:14:35,605 --> 00:14:37,857
You want to pass up
an opportunity like this?

277
00:14:37,940 --> 00:14:39,817
Some people even go into war zones.

278
00:14:39,901 --> 00:14:41,402
Get your act together.

279
00:14:43,029 --> 00:14:44,989
[police sirens approaching]

280
00:14:50,703 --> 00:14:53,831
SPECIAL OPERATIONS UNIT

281
00:14:59,670 --> 00:15:00,671
This way.

282
00:15:02,965 --> 00:15:05,092
-It's right here.
-[Isoo] Over here.

283
00:15:05,176 --> 00:15:06,552
[SOU lead] Step back.

284
00:15:09,513 --> 00:15:11,015
Run an X-ray.

285
00:15:11,098 --> 00:15:12,516
Don't move if you want to live.

286
00:15:16,479 --> 00:15:17,605
DANGER

287
00:15:27,114 --> 00:15:28,699
[device rapidly beeping]

288
00:15:28,783 --> 00:15:30,201
[grunts softly]

289
00:15:34,288 --> 00:15:35,331
[digital beep]

290
00:15:35,414 --> 00:15:36,457
[SOU lead] Explosive confirmed.

291
00:15:37,124 --> 00:15:38,626
There's a pressure plate under the device.

292
00:15:38,709 --> 00:15:39,752
We'll disarm it here.

293
00:15:39,835 --> 00:15:42,171
[♪ tense music playing]

294
00:15:50,346 --> 00:15:51,681
Shh... [groans nervously]

295
00:15:52,598 --> 00:15:54,433
What do I do? How do we...

296
00:16:13,619 --> 00:16:15,329
[♪ suspenseful music intensifies]

297
00:16:22,211 --> 00:16:23,379
Is it done?

298
00:16:23,879 --> 00:16:25,464
-Is it done?
-No.

299
00:16:25,548 --> 00:16:26,882
It'll detonate in 10 seconds.

300
00:16:27,800 --> 00:16:28,926
Huh?

301
00:16:29,010 --> 00:16:30,928
[SOU lead] On three,
run back as fast as you can.

302
00:16:31,012 --> 00:16:32,179
-What?
-[SOU lead] Three.

303
00:16:32,263 --> 00:16:33,431
-Can I let go?
-[SOU lead] Two.

304
00:16:33,514 --> 00:16:34,890
-Bro.
-Do I let go?

305
00:16:34,974 --> 00:16:36,600
-[SOU lead] One.
-Bro, run!

306
00:16:38,227 --> 00:16:39,562
[panting]

307
00:16:39,645 --> 00:16:40,896
[SOU lead chuckling]

308
00:16:44,191 --> 00:16:45,192
Why didn't it go off?

309
00:16:46,819 --> 00:16:48,362
[SOU lead] Device rendered safe.

310
00:16:55,286 --> 00:16:56,454
Hey, nutjob.

311
00:16:58,331 --> 00:16:59,790
I told you to stay out of trouble.
STYLE
::cue()

312
00:17:08,591 --> 00:17:10,176
[♪ upbeat music playing]

313
00:17:10,259 --> 00:17:12,053
-Instructor Joo Hyera?
-[chuckles]

314
00:17:12,136 --> 00:17:14,430
NATIONAL POLICE COUNTERTERRORISM TEAM
TEAM LEADER JOO HYERA

315
00:17:15,681 --> 00:17:16,724
[exhales sharply]

316
00:17:16,807 --> 00:17:19,310
[♪ upbeat music playing]

317
00:17:24,899 --> 00:17:26,400
[upbeat music stops]

318
00:17:26,484 --> 00:17:28,152
[Hyera] Did someone kill your dog?

319
00:17:28,235 --> 00:17:29,612
You think you're John Wick?

320
00:17:29,695 --> 00:17:30,780
Are you Keanu Reeves?

321
00:17:30,863 --> 00:17:31,947
I was just...

322
00:17:32,031 --> 00:17:33,366
[Hyera] Listen up.

323
00:17:36,619 --> 00:17:39,830
You are issued firearms
to protect the public.

324
00:17:40,581 --> 00:17:43,084
Use it only as a last resort,
and use it as safely as possible.

325
00:17:43,876 --> 00:17:45,878
We just have to hit the target, don't we?

326
00:17:47,088 --> 00:17:49,048
So you're the nutjob of this class.

327
00:17:49,131 --> 00:17:50,341
[exhales softly]

328
00:17:52,843 --> 00:17:55,346
[target pulley whirring]

329
00:17:55,429 --> 00:17:56,764
[Isoo sighs]

330
00:17:57,306 --> 00:17:59,517
[in English] My name is John Wick.

331
00:17:59,600 --> 00:18:00,851
[sighs contentedly]

332
00:18:00,935 --> 00:18:03,521
[in Korean] Looks like
a civilian passing by got hit.

333
00:18:03,604 --> 00:18:05,481
-What are you going to do about it?
-Huh?

334
00:18:07,733 --> 00:18:08,901
[Hyera] Eyes forward.

335
00:18:09,151 --> 00:18:10,152
[groans]

336
00:18:10,236 --> 00:18:11,862
[♪ upbeat music playing]

337
00:18:16,575 --> 00:18:18,577
-Stand straight.
-[sighs softly]

338
00:18:20,287 --> 00:18:21,497
Both hands on the gun.

339
00:18:26,460 --> 00:18:27,461
Go sit down.

340
00:18:28,087 --> 00:18:29,088
[sighs]

341
00:18:29,171 --> 00:18:31,215
Shall we try someone tall this time?

342
00:18:31,298 --> 00:18:32,341
Any volunteers?

343
00:18:32,425 --> 00:18:33,801
I'll do it.

344
00:18:33,884 --> 00:18:36,637
[recruits] Ooh!

345
00:18:36,721 --> 00:18:37,763
Jin Isoo, come on up.

346
00:18:40,433 --> 00:18:42,685
-Let's do this!
-[recruits cheering]

347
00:18:48,274 --> 00:18:49,900
Don't come crying even if you get hurt.

348
00:18:49,984 --> 00:18:50,985
All right. Come at me.

349
00:18:51,068 --> 00:18:52,111
[yells]

350
00:18:54,321 --> 00:18:55,322
Oh.

351
00:19:03,247 --> 00:19:04,290
[groans]

352
00:19:04,373 --> 00:19:05,875
You're not crying, are you?

353
00:19:05,958 --> 00:19:07,001
[exhales sharply]

354
00:19:07,918 --> 00:19:10,087
[training officer] You're doing great.
You're almost there.

355
00:19:13,090 --> 00:19:14,133
Hey, nutjob!

356
00:19:14,216 --> 00:19:15,926
You're abandoning your teammates?

357
00:19:16,010 --> 00:19:17,011
[whistle blows]

358
00:19:21,182 --> 00:19:23,267
-Defensive position!
-[recruits] Defensive position!

359
00:19:24,393 --> 00:19:25,728
Advance!

360
00:19:27,229 --> 00:19:28,481
[grunting]

361
00:19:33,194 --> 00:19:34,278
[exclaims]

362
00:19:35,905 --> 00:19:36,989
[grunts]

363
00:19:37,490 --> 00:19:39,450
-[engine revs]
-[tires screeching]

364
00:19:44,538 --> 00:19:45,998
[tires screeching]

365
00:19:52,505 --> 00:19:53,839
Hey, nutjob!

366
00:19:53,923 --> 00:19:55,132
[tires screech]

367
00:19:58,260 --> 00:19:59,428
Back to start!

368
00:20:02,014 --> 00:20:04,892
-[whistle blows]
-[Isoo] Seven, eight, nine.

369
00:20:04,975 --> 00:20:05,976
[whistle blows]

370
00:20:06,894 --> 00:20:08,103
[whistle blows]

371
00:20:08,979 --> 00:20:10,856
Hey, nutjob. Do it properly.

372
00:20:13,442 --> 00:20:15,528
-Jeez, I lost count.
-[whistle blows]

373
00:20:16,195 --> 00:20:17,363
[whistle blows rhythmically]

374
00:20:20,783 --> 00:20:21,951
[whistle echoes]

375
00:20:24,078 --> 00:20:25,287
[Isoo] That instructor from hell...

376
00:20:25,371 --> 00:20:26,622
It's her?

377
00:20:27,206 --> 00:20:28,749
But she's with Counterterrorism.

378
00:20:29,917 --> 00:20:32,419
She was filling in
for an instructor on sick leave.

379
00:20:32,503 --> 00:20:33,838
She hates me.

380
00:20:35,089 --> 00:20:36,298
[sighs wearily]

381
00:20:36,382 --> 00:20:38,217
God, the trauma. [sighs]

382
00:20:41,637 --> 00:20:42,721
[sighs]
STYLE
::cue()

383
00:20:46,642 --> 00:20:47,685
SPECIALIST

384
00:20:47,768 --> 00:20:50,145
-[Isoo] My leg's killing me.
-[Kyungjin] Your leg? Let me massage it.

385
00:20:50,229 --> 00:20:51,647
-[Isoo] No, the right leg.
-[Kyungjin] The other one.

386
00:20:51,730 --> 00:20:52,898
[grunts on screen]

387
00:20:52,982 --> 00:20:54,191
-[Kyungjin] Here? Down below?
-[Isoo] Now, the left.

388
00:20:54,275 --> 00:20:55,276
[Kyungjin] The left.

389
00:20:55,818 --> 00:20:57,361
-[Kyungjin] Down below?
-[Isoo] Yeah, down below.

390
00:20:57,444 --> 00:20:59,280
We can't use this clip of Jin Isoo.

391
00:20:59,363 --> 00:21:00,614
He looks like an idiot.

392
00:21:01,574 --> 00:21:03,576
-Then what do we do?
-[keyboard clacks]

393
00:21:03,659 --> 00:21:04,660
[sighs in exasperation]

394
00:21:04,743 --> 00:21:06,871
But this is such a great story.

395
00:21:08,497 --> 00:21:09,623
[keyboard clacks]

396
00:21:11,792 --> 00:21:13,127
[♪ quirky music playing]

397
00:21:13,210 --> 00:21:14,336
[keyboard clacks]

398
00:21:17,965 --> 00:21:19,008
Hey.

399
00:21:19,091 --> 00:21:21,552
Send the footage of Jin Isoo
to the news team.

400
00:21:21,635 --> 00:21:23,137
But what about our story?

401
00:21:23,220 --> 00:21:24,471
[keyboard clacks]

402
00:21:29,268 --> 00:21:30,269
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

403
00:21:30,352 --> 00:21:32,146
[news anchor 1] Earlier today,
a homemade bomb was discovered

404
00:21:32,229 --> 00:21:33,814
at Hansu Department Store.

405
00:21:33,898 --> 00:21:36,734
The billionaire heir
and detective of Gangha Police Station,

406
00:21:36,817 --> 00:21:39,403
Detective Jin Isoo,
discovered the explosive.

407
00:21:39,486 --> 00:21:42,573
[news anchor 2] He seems frozen
in the footage. What transpired?

408
00:21:42,656 --> 00:21:45,326
[news anchor 1] Detective Jin didn't know
it was a bomb

409
00:21:45,409 --> 00:21:46,660
and triggered it by accident.

410
00:21:46,744 --> 00:21:49,872
[news anchor 2] And why is he reacting
like that? The bomb didn't even go off.

411
00:21:49,955 --> 00:21:51,332
If you look at the footage--

412
00:21:51,415 --> 00:21:52,583
[sighs in exasperation]

413
00:21:53,500 --> 00:21:55,502
-Chief Park.
-Yes, sir.

414
00:21:56,295 --> 00:21:58,631
I didn't want to come here.

415
00:22:00,382 --> 00:22:02,301
Because of Jin Isoo.

416
00:22:02,801 --> 00:22:05,095
If I'd had another option,
I wouldn't be here.

417
00:22:05,179 --> 00:22:06,263
Yes, sir.

418
00:22:06,347 --> 00:22:08,474
The head of the police station retired,

419
00:22:08,557 --> 00:22:10,184
and his team leader went abroad,

420
00:22:10,768 --> 00:22:13,187
so what is he still doing here?

421
00:22:13,270 --> 00:22:14,271
He's a chaebol heir.

422
00:22:14,355 --> 00:22:16,732
He should be running the company
or off somewhere enjoying himself.

423
00:22:16,815 --> 00:22:18,400
So why?

424
00:22:18,484 --> 00:22:19,652
Because he's a detective.

425
00:22:21,695 --> 00:22:24,865
I hate to admit it,
but Jin Isoo is a good detective.

426
00:22:24,949 --> 00:22:27,618
Right, he's a good detective,

427
00:22:27,701 --> 00:22:30,537
so he's earned himself
two excessive force complaints

428
00:22:30,621 --> 00:22:32,289
and three civil lawsuits.

429
00:22:32,373 --> 00:22:35,167
[chuckles] These were all cleared, sir.

430
00:22:35,250 --> 00:22:36,377
Chief Park.

431
00:22:37,127 --> 00:22:39,254
Come to your senses.

432
00:22:40,381 --> 00:22:44,843
He's nothing but trouble for our station.

433
00:22:45,678 --> 00:22:48,764
I've been here less than a month,
and he's already screwed up.

434
00:22:48,847 --> 00:22:50,015
What are you going to do?

435
00:22:50,099 --> 00:22:53,018
The Counterterrorism Team
will assess the bomb

436
00:22:53,102 --> 00:22:55,104
and work with
the Violent Crime Investigation Team 1.

437
00:22:55,187 --> 00:22:57,564
The Cybercrime Team
is tracking down who sent the DM.

438
00:22:58,315 --> 00:23:00,317
[sighs] God, I...

439
00:23:00,985 --> 00:23:04,530
Why haven't you found them
a new team leader?

440
00:23:05,114 --> 00:23:07,408
Because no one wants the job.

441
00:23:07,491 --> 00:23:08,909
See?

442
00:23:09,410 --> 00:23:11,870
Who'd want to manage
a rich kid who was handed the job?

443
00:23:11,954 --> 00:23:13,122
Huh?

444
00:23:13,205 --> 00:23:15,207
I'll keep looking, sir.

445
00:23:15,290 --> 00:23:18,127
Just focus on the investigation.

446
00:23:18,210 --> 00:23:19,294
Go catch the guy!

447
00:23:19,378 --> 00:23:21,880
Yes, sir.

448
00:23:23,048 --> 00:23:24,425
[sighs in exasperation]

449
00:23:24,883 --> 00:23:27,428
[news anchor 1] Earlier today,
a homemade bomb was discovered

450
00:23:27,511 --> 00:23:28,971
at Hansu Department Store.

451
00:23:29,054 --> 00:23:32,141
The billionaire heir
and detective of Gangha Police Station,

452
00:23:32,224 --> 00:23:33,767
Detective Jin Isoo,
discovered the explosive...

453
00:23:33,851 --> 00:23:35,269
[groans] My leg's numb.

454
00:23:36,020 --> 00:23:37,312
I can't bear it anymore!

455
00:23:38,022 --> 00:23:39,314
You can't.

456
00:23:39,398 --> 00:23:41,108
It'll go off if you move!

457
00:23:41,859 --> 00:23:43,318
[news anchor 2] And why is he
reacting like that?

458
00:23:43,402 --> 00:23:44,528
The bomb didn't even go off.

459
00:23:44,611 --> 00:23:45,612
-Three minutes.
-Thanks.

460
00:23:45,696 --> 00:23:47,114
[Byungsik, in English] Okay.

461
00:23:48,490 --> 00:23:50,826
[in Korean] Turn the TV off!
We're on duty.

462
00:23:51,827 --> 00:23:53,287
-That's not funny.
-Bro!

463
00:23:53,370 --> 00:23:56,081
VIOLENT CRIME INVESTIGATION TEAM 1
PARK JUNYOUNG

464
00:23:56,165 --> 00:23:57,875
I told you not to make fun of him.

465
00:23:57,958 --> 00:23:59,418
[chuckles softly]

466
00:23:59,501 --> 00:24:01,879
How could I not? It's too entertaining.

467
00:24:01,962 --> 00:24:03,297
This one's good for 10 years.

468
00:24:11,889 --> 00:24:13,599
MR. CHOI
INCOMING CALL

469
00:24:13,682 --> 00:24:15,601
[cell phone ringing through car audio]

470
00:24:16,685 --> 00:24:18,187
Hi, Mr. Choi.

471
00:24:18,270 --> 00:24:19,271
Detective Jin.

472
00:24:20,189 --> 00:24:22,316
What happened? Are you all right?

473
00:24:22,399 --> 00:24:25,194
I'm not all right.
I'm so embarrassed I could die.

474
00:24:25,277 --> 00:24:26,361
[sighs]

475
00:24:26,737 --> 00:24:28,030
As long as you weren't hurt.

476
00:24:28,113 --> 00:24:30,324
There's nothing wrong
with being embarrassed.

477
00:24:35,662 --> 00:24:37,039
[Isoo sighs]

478
00:24:37,498 --> 00:24:38,707
You're the great Jin Isoo.

479
00:24:38,791 --> 00:24:40,584
Are you really going to let this
get to you?

480
00:24:40,667 --> 00:24:42,795
He's right, bro. Cheer up.

481
00:24:42,878 --> 00:24:45,005
You guys didn't make the news.

482
00:24:45,089 --> 00:24:47,716
The most humiliating moment
of my life is on TV right now.

483
00:24:47,800 --> 00:24:49,885
Come on, bro. People will forget about it.

484
00:24:49,968 --> 00:24:52,137
Forget? They won't forget.

485
00:24:52,221 --> 00:24:53,222
This'll last a decade.

486
00:24:56,809 --> 00:25:01,105
Then again, your ex slapping you
on Gangnam-daero was four years ago.

487
00:25:01,188 --> 00:25:02,773
Is that still going around?

488
00:25:02,856 --> 00:25:04,691
Then this might last forever.

489
00:25:04,775 --> 00:25:05,776
[gasps]

490
00:25:07,194 --> 00:25:09,488
You should just carve it
into your tombstone.

491
00:25:09,571 --> 00:25:11,198
"The man who triggered a bomb."

492
00:25:11,281 --> 00:25:12,449
[laughing]

493
00:25:14,952 --> 00:25:15,953
Bro.

494
00:25:18,163 --> 00:25:19,665
-Hey, where are you going?
-Bro.

495
00:25:19,748 --> 00:25:20,999
-Hey, Bomb Guy.
-Bro!

496
00:25:21,083 --> 00:25:22,209
[Junyoung] Wait up!

497
00:25:22,835 --> 00:25:23,919
Bomb Guy.

498
00:25:24,002 --> 00:25:25,796
-Come on.
-Bro.

499
00:25:27,297 --> 00:25:28,799
How many times is this now?

500
00:25:28,882 --> 00:25:30,592
-Also...
-You're laughing?

501
00:25:31,593 --> 00:25:33,303
You're seriously laughing right now?

502
00:25:34,763 --> 00:25:35,806
Sorry.

503
00:25:36,306 --> 00:25:39,518
The news team kept begging us,
saying it was a huge scoop.

504
00:25:40,227 --> 00:25:41,311
-Sorry.
-Sorry.

505
00:25:41,854 --> 00:25:44,398
Even so, you made me look
like a complete idiot.
STYLE
::cue()

506
00:25:44,481 --> 00:25:45,774
In that kind of situation,

507
00:25:45,858 --> 00:25:48,318
anyone would have looked like an idiot.

508
00:25:50,904 --> 00:25:52,865
Are you mocking me right now?

509
00:25:52,948 --> 00:25:55,159
Or are you trying to rub it in?
Which is it?

510
00:25:58,078 --> 00:25:59,079
She's coming. Let's go.

511
00:26:01,165 --> 00:26:02,624
[♪ dramatic music playing]

512
00:26:16,221 --> 00:26:17,681
They've moved on to her, haven't they?

513
00:26:18,682 --> 00:26:20,684
Well, she is pretty cool.

514
00:26:20,767 --> 00:26:21,935
I'm a fan too now.

515
00:26:22,811 --> 00:26:24,271
Are you moving on to her too?

516
00:26:24,354 --> 00:26:25,689
-We'll see.
-"We'll see"?

517
00:26:25,772 --> 00:26:26,940
"We'll see"?

518
00:26:27,024 --> 00:26:28,025
That little...

519
00:26:28,775 --> 00:26:30,527
Hang in there, nutjob.

520
00:26:31,111 --> 00:26:32,112
What the...

521
00:26:34,281 --> 00:26:35,490
This is ridiculous.

522
00:26:35,574 --> 00:26:37,492
Ugh. My head hurts.

523
00:26:37,576 --> 00:26:38,577
Jeez.

524
00:26:39,328 --> 00:26:40,329
[sighs]

525
00:26:40,412 --> 00:26:42,080
[♪ quirky music playing]

526
00:26:42,164 --> 00:26:43,582
PRIEST, BREADTH, TAN (HEX CODE)

527
00:26:43,665 --> 00:26:44,917
PHOTO EVIDENCE 3, BOMB X-RAY

528
00:26:45,000 --> 00:26:46,877
HANSU DEPARTMENT STORE
ATTEMPTED BOMBING

529
00:26:46,960 --> 00:26:50,255
The bomb appears to have been made
with ammonium nitrate.

530
00:26:50,339 --> 00:26:51,715
It's a simple design.

531
00:26:51,798 --> 00:26:54,843
It detonates when the button
is pressed and then released.

532
00:26:54,927 --> 00:26:58,222
A bomb design like this
is all over the dark web.

533
00:26:58,305 --> 00:27:00,933
Which means it will be difficult
to identify a suspect.

534
00:27:01,934 --> 00:27:03,101
Anything on your end?

535
00:27:03,185 --> 00:27:06,104
Right, we checked
all the security cameras in the building,

536
00:27:06,188 --> 00:27:09,066
but there's too much foot traffic,
and the cameras are too far away

537
00:27:09,149 --> 00:27:10,442
to identify the suspect.

538
00:27:10,525 --> 00:27:12,444
The account that sent the DM was fake too.

539
00:27:13,487 --> 00:27:14,863
I'm sure it was.

540
00:27:14,947 --> 00:27:16,990
No fingerprints were found on the device.

541
00:27:17,074 --> 00:27:20,077
Based on our analysis,
there wasn't much ammonium nitrate.

542
00:27:20,160 --> 00:27:23,372
Even if it had gone off, the blast radius
would've been about a meter.

543
00:27:24,831 --> 00:27:28,919
In other words, it wasn't much of a bomb.
Right? Okay.

544
00:27:32,214 --> 00:27:35,008
If we hadn't defused it in time,
you would've lost your hands.

545
00:27:36,009 --> 00:27:38,136
Think before you start touching things.

546
00:27:42,224 --> 00:27:44,768
If I'd known it was a bomb,
I wouldn't have touched it.

547
00:27:44,851 --> 00:27:46,103
Why didn't you know?

548
00:27:46,728 --> 00:27:48,063
You were given all the clues.

549
00:27:54,236 --> 00:27:55,320
What're you looking at?

550
00:27:57,531 --> 00:28:00,534
Ma'am, we came up
with a whole new concept.

551
00:28:00,617 --> 00:28:03,286
There's no need for that.
I'm not going to go on camera.

552
00:28:03,954 --> 00:28:05,372
Please delete everything you filmed today.

553
00:28:05,455 --> 00:28:09,835
But if you were in it,
it'd help the police's image.

554
00:28:10,335 --> 00:28:11,795
I don't have time,

555
00:28:11,878 --> 00:28:14,172
and I don't want my face out there.

556
00:28:14,256 --> 00:28:15,632
Please delete the footage.

557
00:28:20,095 --> 00:28:21,596
What do we do?

558
00:28:22,097 --> 00:28:24,099
We have nothing for next week's show.

559
00:28:25,225 --> 00:28:26,435
I know.

560
00:28:27,728 --> 00:28:28,729
I said, I know.

561
00:28:29,187 --> 00:28:32,065
[sighs] This reminds me of that saying,

562
00:28:32,149 --> 00:28:35,068
"Better the devil you know." [sighs]

563
00:28:35,152 --> 00:28:37,029
The ship's sailed. Now you're in trouble.

564
00:28:37,112 --> 00:28:39,031
[clicking tongue] Bet you miss me now.

565
00:28:42,701 --> 00:28:43,702
What?

566
00:28:52,836 --> 00:28:53,962
[door opens]

567
00:28:54,838 --> 00:28:55,839
[door closes]

568
00:28:59,092 --> 00:29:00,093
Hey, Joo.

569
00:29:01,428 --> 00:29:02,429
Sir.

570
00:29:02,512 --> 00:29:03,764
It's been a while.

571
00:29:03,847 --> 00:29:05,557
[chuckles] It has.

572
00:29:05,640 --> 00:29:06,683
Coffee?

573
00:29:07,893 --> 00:29:10,228
-[chuckles]
-How have you been?

574
00:29:10,312 --> 00:29:12,814
Oh. Same old, same old.

575
00:29:12,898 --> 00:29:14,733
I miss being out in the field.

576
00:29:15,942 --> 00:29:19,029
I heard you've been doing great
over there in SOU.

577
00:29:19,112 --> 00:29:20,781
[chuckling]

578
00:29:20,864 --> 00:29:22,741
-It's all thanks to you.
-So you do know.

579
00:29:22,824 --> 00:29:24,785
[both chuckle]

580
00:29:24,868 --> 00:29:26,411
How does it feel to be back here?

581
00:29:27,788 --> 00:29:29,456
It really takes me back.

582
00:29:29,539 --> 00:29:31,166
Gangha is like home to me.

583
00:29:32,250 --> 00:29:33,502
Guess I'll be seeing you around.

584
00:29:34,086 --> 00:29:35,337
Yes.

585
00:29:35,420 --> 00:29:37,506
My team is going to work here for a while.

586
00:29:38,090 --> 00:29:40,217
Detective Jin Isoo needs protection too.

587
00:29:40,300 --> 00:29:42,761
Sure. Team 1 doesn't have
a leader right now,

588
00:29:42,844 --> 00:29:44,763
so I'll leave the case in your hands.

589
00:29:44,846 --> 00:29:45,847
All right.

590
00:29:46,890 --> 00:29:48,892
It might just be a prank,

591
00:29:48,975 --> 00:29:51,186
but someone
could actually be after Jin Isoo.

592
00:29:51,269 --> 00:29:52,687
I know.

593
00:29:54,147 --> 00:29:56,233
You need to catch the suspect quickly.

594
00:29:57,067 --> 00:29:58,068
Got it.

595
00:30:04,282 --> 00:30:05,575
[sighs]

596
00:30:10,497 --> 00:30:12,624
Can I let go? Do I let go?

597
00:30:12,707 --> 00:30:14,000
[Kyungjin] Bro, run!

598
00:30:14,501 --> 00:30:15,794
[Hyera] Hey, nutjob.

599
00:30:15,877 --> 00:30:17,337
I told you to stay out of trouble.

600
00:30:17,420 --> 00:30:19,089
[♪ upbeat hip-hop music playing]

601
00:30:21,883 --> 00:30:22,968
Eyes forward.

602
00:30:24,219 --> 00:30:25,846
You're not crying, are you?

603
00:30:26,429 --> 00:30:27,681
[Isoo] That instructor from hell...

604
00:30:27,764 --> 00:30:29,141
[Kyungjin] It's her?

605
00:30:29,224 --> 00:30:30,559
Hey, nutjob!

606
00:30:30,642 --> 00:30:32,811
Think before you start touching things.
STYLE
::cue()

607
00:30:46,408 --> 00:30:47,576
[cell phone vibrates]

608
00:30:49,119 --> 00:30:51,955
[Hyeonwoo] Please forgive us
and answer your phone.

609
00:30:52,038 --> 00:30:53,665
[Jaeeun] We weren't thinking straight.

610
00:30:53,748 --> 00:30:54,916
[cell phone vibrating]

611
00:30:55,000 --> 00:30:57,586
SBC DIRECTOR KANG JAEEUN

612
00:30:57,669 --> 00:30:58,670
Jeez.

613
00:31:00,297 --> 00:31:03,049
[sighs] Why are you being so clingy? Huh?

614
00:31:05,886 --> 00:31:09,222
Well, I do have an event today
that would make for good content.

615
00:31:10,974 --> 00:31:13,727
Okay, fine. Then write up a new contract.

616
00:31:13,810 --> 00:31:17,355
Nothing goes on air
until I've seen the final edit.

617
00:31:18,607 --> 00:31:20,483
Okay. Bye.

618
00:31:22,402 --> 00:31:23,403
[line disconnects]

619
00:31:26,448 --> 00:31:28,867
We're leading
this investigation as of today.

620
00:31:29,951 --> 00:31:31,369
We don't need any desks.

621
00:31:32,120 --> 00:31:33,622
We'll use the conference table.

622
00:31:40,837 --> 00:31:43,173
She thinks she's some big-shot
team leader, doesn't she?

623
00:31:44,466 --> 00:31:46,843
-I'm heading out first. Dress sharp.
-[Junyoung] Okay.

624
00:31:46,927 --> 00:31:48,887
Detective Jin, where are you going?

625
00:31:51,389 --> 00:31:53,516
I have a launch event today.

626
00:31:53,600 --> 00:31:56,186
-A launch event?
-For a whiskey I developed.

627
00:31:57,854 --> 00:31:59,731
Don't you know moonlighting's prohibited?

628
00:32:00,315 --> 00:32:03,109
I started it four years ago
but quit when I became a cop.

629
00:32:03,193 --> 00:32:04,361
Don't go.

630
00:32:05,111 --> 00:32:06,321
What?

631
00:32:06,404 --> 00:32:07,906
[♪ dramatic music playing]

632
00:32:08,448 --> 00:32:10,784
-But I'm the star of the event.
-Then push it back.

633
00:32:10,867 --> 00:32:11,952
[scoffs]

634
00:32:13,703 --> 00:32:15,038
[sighs deeply]

635
00:32:15,997 --> 00:32:19,167
Do I still look like
a recruit to you? Huh?

636
00:32:27,384 --> 00:32:28,385
Is that an order?

637
00:32:28,468 --> 00:32:31,638
I've been assigned to lead this case.
Didn't you get the memo?

638
00:32:32,639 --> 00:32:33,640
I did.

639
00:32:33,723 --> 00:32:35,976
We still haven't identified
a bombing suspect.

640
00:32:36,476 --> 00:32:37,602
They might be after you.

641
00:32:38,395 --> 00:32:41,273
It's probably a prank.
They even gave us clues.

642
00:32:41,356 --> 00:32:43,441
It was just to humiliate me,

643
00:32:44,025 --> 00:32:46,528
and it was a huge success thanks to you.

644
00:32:46,611 --> 00:32:48,905
Besides, I've always had
people out to kill me.

645
00:32:48,989 --> 00:32:50,031
Why?

646
00:32:50,115 --> 00:32:51,283
Just, you know,

647
00:32:51,783 --> 00:32:53,410
for petty reasons.

648
00:32:55,287 --> 00:32:57,747
All the more reason to be careful.
Don't go.

649
00:32:58,957 --> 00:33:03,461
My security team
is checking every box, so just let it go.

650
00:33:04,629 --> 00:33:06,756
I'll handle it, okay?

651
00:33:08,091 --> 00:33:09,092
See you guys later.

652
00:33:10,010 --> 00:33:11,011
[sighs softly]

653
00:33:16,808 --> 00:33:18,059
-[door closes]
-[clears throat]

654
00:33:18,143 --> 00:33:19,144
We will

655
00:33:21,021 --> 00:33:22,439
keep an eye on him.

656
00:33:22,522 --> 00:33:23,565
Right.

657
00:33:24,357 --> 00:33:25,358
We'll watch over him.

658
00:33:29,237 --> 00:33:30,405
-[sighs]
-[door closes]

659
00:33:36,077 --> 00:33:38,330
[♪ elegant piano music playing]

660
00:33:58,516 --> 00:34:00,143
[♪ upbeat rock music playing]
STYLE
::cue()

661
00:34:01,061 --> 00:34:02,437
[crowd cheering]

662
00:34:05,315 --> 00:34:07,984
-Jin Isoo!
-Jin Isoo!

663
00:34:08,777 --> 00:34:10,945
-Jin Isoo!
-Jin Isoo!

664
00:34:25,502 --> 00:34:26,503
[in English] Cheers.

665
00:34:27,128 --> 00:34:28,880
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

666
00:34:33,093 --> 00:34:34,427
[exhales contentedly]

667
00:34:37,931 --> 00:34:38,932
Bang!

668
00:34:39,015 --> 00:34:40,100
[giggles]

669
00:34:43,561 --> 00:34:44,562
Oh?

670
00:34:45,313 --> 00:34:46,523
Kwaktube.

671
00:34:47,023 --> 00:34:48,900
[in Korean] I thought
you'd be too busy to come.

672
00:34:48,983 --> 00:34:50,568
-No way.
-You're looking good.

673
00:34:50,652 --> 00:34:52,195
Oh, come on.

674
00:34:52,278 --> 00:34:53,363
By the way,

675
00:34:53,446 --> 00:34:54,823
isn't your wife due soon?

676
00:34:54,906 --> 00:34:56,282
She's actually due tomorrow.

677
00:34:56,366 --> 00:34:57,367
[gasps]

678
00:34:57,659 --> 00:34:58,743
[cell phone vibrating]

679
00:35:00,161 --> 00:35:02,038
-The hospital...
-The hospital?

680
00:35:02,872 --> 00:35:03,873
Hello?

681
00:35:04,624 --> 00:35:06,042
Yes. What?

682
00:35:07,544 --> 00:35:08,628
I need to go right now.

683
00:35:08,712 --> 00:35:09,879
Right now?

684
00:35:09,963 --> 00:35:10,964
The baby's coming.

685
00:35:11,047 --> 00:35:12,090
The baby...

686
00:35:14,259 --> 00:35:15,552
Good luck!

687
00:35:16,594 --> 00:35:18,888
[sighs] Hope the baby
doesn't take after the dad.

688
00:35:19,556 --> 00:35:21,224
Ah. I'm the one who made this.

689
00:35:21,307 --> 00:35:23,435
The logo is the defining feature,
you get...

690
00:35:23,977 --> 00:35:24,978
Hold on.

691
00:35:26,062 --> 00:35:27,897
[sighs] Clothes do make the man.

692
00:35:27,981 --> 00:35:28,982
What?

693
00:35:29,441 --> 00:35:31,192
[in English] Oh, oh. Stop.

694
00:35:33,903 --> 00:35:35,155
[in Korean] What are you doing here?

695
00:35:35,238 --> 00:35:36,364
I didn't invite you.

696
00:35:36,948 --> 00:35:38,032
I'm going to check inside.

697
00:35:38,116 --> 00:35:40,744
There's no need. You're embarrassing me.

698
00:35:41,828 --> 00:35:43,705
You can't be here dressed like that.

699
00:35:43,788 --> 00:35:45,457
Ever heard of a dress code?

700
00:35:46,291 --> 00:35:47,375
You two, head inside.

701
00:35:48,084 --> 00:35:49,085
Go.

702
00:35:49,669 --> 00:35:50,920
Security.

703
00:35:52,672 --> 00:35:55,049
Get her out of here, okay?
Dress code violation.

704
00:35:55,133 --> 00:35:56,384
-Hey, Jin Isoo.
-Let's go.

705
00:35:56,468 --> 00:35:58,386
Wait, Jin Isoo... [sighs]

706
00:36:00,263 --> 00:36:02,182
[exclaims] That damn nutjob.

707
00:36:12,817 --> 00:36:14,235
What happened?

708
00:36:14,319 --> 00:36:15,570
It's nothing.

709
00:36:24,162 --> 00:36:25,163
Keep watch.

710
00:36:25,246 --> 00:36:26,956
[♪ smooth jazz music playing]

711
00:36:34,547 --> 00:36:35,673
[Isoo] Mmm.

712
00:36:39,302 --> 00:36:40,970
Oh, this smells great.

713
00:36:41,054 --> 00:36:44,307
Right? There's a subtle hint of vanilla.

714
00:36:44,390 --> 00:36:45,433
Try it. Cheers.

715
00:36:45,517 --> 00:36:46,518
[glasses clink]

716
00:36:49,646 --> 00:36:51,856
I'll drink it later, just in case.

717
00:36:53,817 --> 00:36:55,735
Me too. We need to protect you.

718
00:36:56,486 --> 00:36:58,112
I told you, it's fine.

719
00:36:58,196 --> 00:37:00,406
I don't need protecting. [sighs]

720
00:37:05,328 --> 00:37:06,579
Oh...

721
00:37:06,663 --> 00:37:09,332
That's what your job does to you.
She can't switch off.

722
00:37:11,084 --> 00:37:12,085
[scoffs]

723
00:37:13,670 --> 00:37:15,171
[sighs] Whatever. Just ignore her.
STYLE
::cue()

724
00:37:20,343 --> 00:37:23,513
See? I told you nothing would happen.

725
00:37:23,596 --> 00:37:26,558
You guys didn't get a taste,
so I'll send you a whole box.

726
00:37:26,641 --> 00:37:28,101
Awesome.

727
00:37:29,435 --> 00:37:30,478
[Jaeeun] Thanks for today.

728
00:37:31,187 --> 00:37:33,022
I'll call you after we're done editing.

729
00:37:33,606 --> 00:37:35,149
Make sure I look cool, okay?

730
00:37:35,733 --> 00:37:36,734
-Okay.
-Good.

731
00:37:41,656 --> 00:37:42,949
Oh, no.

732
00:37:43,533 --> 00:37:45,535
Guess you couldn't find the bomb.

733
00:37:46,786 --> 00:37:48,079
Have a drink before you go.

734
00:37:48,746 --> 00:37:50,623
-No.
-[Isoo] Suit yourself.

735
00:37:51,207 --> 00:37:53,251
You're going home, right?
Where do you live?

736
00:37:53,334 --> 00:37:54,335
[scoffs]

737
00:37:56,004 --> 00:37:57,088
Noblesse.

738
00:37:57,171 --> 00:37:59,173
Don't wander around. Go straight home.

739
00:37:59,257 --> 00:38:01,259
-[sighs in exasperation]
-[cell phone vibrates]

740
00:38:06,598 --> 00:38:09,350
[♪ ominous music playing]

741
00:38:12,520 --> 00:38:14,689
[distorted voice] Detective Jin,
did you think the game was over?

742
00:38:14,772 --> 00:38:15,773
Round 2.

743
00:38:25,325 --> 00:38:27,285
[♪ intense music playing]

744
00:38:33,166 --> 00:38:34,542
What on earth?

745
00:38:48,348 --> 00:38:49,641
[glass shattering]

746
00:38:55,188 --> 00:38:57,941
[Isoo breathing heavily]

747
00:38:58,900 --> 00:39:00,777
[Hyera whimpering]

748
00:39:03,488 --> 00:39:05,740
-Are you okay?
-Yeah. You?

749
00:39:06,783 --> 00:39:07,909
[Junyoung] Kyungjin, you okay?

750
00:39:08,910 --> 00:39:10,078
Yeah, I'm fine.

751
00:39:14,207 --> 00:39:15,750
[breathing heavily]

752
00:39:22,340 --> 00:39:24,092
[sighs]

753
00:39:29,931 --> 00:39:31,516
[indistinct conversation]

754
00:39:40,066 --> 00:39:41,859
[♪ tense music continues]

755
00:39:56,749 --> 00:39:58,793
-[sighs]
-[cell phone vibrates]

756
00:40:06,926 --> 00:40:09,512
[♪ ominous music playing]

757
00:40:10,096 --> 00:40:11,597
[distorted voice] Detective Jin,
you got lucky.

758
00:40:13,558 --> 00:40:15,309
[disembodied malicious laughter]

759
00:40:17,603 --> 00:40:21,190
[news anchor] Another homemade bomb attack
has occurred in the heart of Seoul.

760
00:40:21,274 --> 00:40:25,361
Once again, Detective Jin Isoo
was at the center of the attack,

761
00:40:25,445 --> 00:40:30,324
as the attack took place at a venue
where he was hosting an event.

762
00:40:30,408 --> 00:40:34,620
Police say the suspect's motive
remains unknown.

763
00:40:34,704 --> 00:40:36,998
[♪ music swells, fades]

764
00:40:39,083 --> 00:40:41,002
[Junyoung] Thank you for your cooperation.

765
00:40:45,423 --> 00:40:47,300
Did you get the full staff and guest list?

766
00:40:47,383 --> 00:40:49,052
Yes, they just faxed it over.

767
00:40:51,137 --> 00:40:52,430
And the list of YouTubers?

768
00:40:52,513 --> 00:40:53,890
They'll check and send it over.

769
00:40:53,973 --> 00:40:56,642
Check the security footage
and identify anyone suspicious.

770
00:40:56,726 --> 00:40:57,727
-Got it.
-[Junyoung] Got it.
STYLE
::cue()

771
00:41:03,066 --> 00:41:05,359
[sighs] It's out of the camera's view.

772
00:41:06,819 --> 00:41:08,905
-[Junyoung] Is this all the footage?
-Yes.

773
00:41:10,698 --> 00:41:14,118
I'll check around the building.
You chase the YouTubers for their footage.

774
00:41:14,202 --> 00:41:15,244
Got it.

775
00:41:19,957 --> 00:41:22,335
[distorted voice] Detective Jin.
Let the game begin.

776
00:41:22,418 --> 00:41:23,544
[glass shattering]

777
00:41:23,628 --> 00:41:24,837
I have a gift for you.

778
00:41:24,921 --> 00:41:26,339
-[high-pitched ringing]
-[device beeping]

779
00:41:26,422 --> 00:41:27,423
-Don't touch that!
-[Kyungjin] Bro!

780
00:41:27,507 --> 00:41:28,925
[distorted voice] Did you think
the game was over?

781
00:41:31,219 --> 00:41:32,470
Detective Jin, you got lucky.

782
00:41:32,553 --> 00:41:34,388
[tinkling]

783
00:41:37,433 --> 00:41:39,393
[high-pitched ringing swells]

784
00:41:41,938 --> 00:41:43,815
-[high-pitched ringing stops]
-[gasps, panting]

785
00:41:44,398 --> 00:41:45,775
Are you okay?

786
00:41:46,526 --> 00:41:48,736
[panting heavily]

787
00:41:51,405 --> 00:41:52,615
So...

788
00:41:52,698 --> 00:41:55,660
Is someone trying to kill you?

789
00:41:59,789 --> 00:42:00,998
You should stop filming now.

790
00:42:01,707 --> 00:42:03,543
But we signed a contract.

791
00:42:05,336 --> 00:42:07,880
You are no longer allowed in this office.
Please leave.

792
00:42:09,382 --> 00:42:10,675
[breath trembles]

793
00:42:17,974 --> 00:42:19,308
Detective Jin, a word?

794
00:42:20,393 --> 00:42:22,270
[♪ tense music playing]

795
00:42:25,523 --> 00:42:28,151
Write up a list of people
who might want to kill you.

796
00:42:29,402 --> 00:42:33,447
I didn't mean that literally.
No one actually wants me dead.

797
00:42:33,531 --> 00:42:34,907
Doesn't matter how trivial.

798
00:42:34,991 --> 00:42:36,534
Write down anyone who hates you

799
00:42:36,617 --> 00:42:38,411
or anyone you've hurt.

800
00:42:38,494 --> 00:42:39,704
Everyone you can think of.

801
00:42:40,371 --> 00:42:42,290
It doesn't take much to hold a grudge.

802
00:42:42,373 --> 00:42:43,416
[sighs]

803
00:42:50,381 --> 00:42:51,591
Jin Isoo.

804
00:42:52,800 --> 00:42:55,553
Using a homemade bomb
means they have nothing to lose.

805
00:42:56,220 --> 00:42:57,388
They don't care if they die.

806
00:42:59,765 --> 00:43:02,518
That's how determined they are
to kill you.

807
00:43:08,733 --> 00:43:11,402
A pager was used
in the Seongje bombing three years ago.

808
00:43:11,485 --> 00:43:12,778
That's right.

809
00:43:12,862 --> 00:43:15,156
Ask for the file.
He should be out of prison by now.

810
00:43:15,990 --> 00:43:17,200
Yes, ma'am.

811
00:43:18,034 --> 00:43:19,744
[Kyungjin] I got the footage
from the YouTubers.

812
00:43:20,536 --> 00:43:21,537
[mouse clicks]

813
00:43:21,621 --> 00:43:23,706
[♪ foreboding music playing]

814
00:43:24,540 --> 00:43:25,541
[keyboard clacks]

815
00:43:36,510 --> 00:43:38,304
He seems suspicious.

816
00:43:38,387 --> 00:43:39,847
-Wait.
-[keyboard clacks]

817
00:43:51,692 --> 00:43:52,693
NOH JINSU, AGE 27

818
00:43:52,777 --> 00:43:55,196
-It's him. Noh Jinsu, age 27.
-Right.

819
00:43:55,279 --> 00:43:56,739
[keyboard clacking]

820
00:43:56,822 --> 00:43:59,200
IDENTITY SEARCH
NOH JINSU

821
00:44:05,373 --> 00:44:09,126
His father worked at Hansu Chemical
and left eight months ago.

822
00:44:09,210 --> 00:44:12,171
-What's his address?
-17-38 Yongpae-dong.

823
00:44:12,964 --> 00:44:14,215
-Let's go.
-[Kyungjin] Okay.

824
00:44:17,426 --> 00:44:20,930
[officer] I checked the Seongje bombing.
Park Gyeongtae has indeed been released.

825
00:44:22,306 --> 00:44:23,432
Let's go check him out.

826
00:44:23,516 --> 00:44:24,517
-Yes, ma'am.
-Yes, ma'am.

827
00:44:25,059 --> 00:44:27,436
We identified a suspicious waiter.

828
00:44:27,520 --> 00:44:29,897
We're going to see someone
who built a similar bomb.

829
00:44:30,481 --> 00:44:31,691
We'll go check on the waiter.

830
00:44:31,774 --> 00:44:34,110
Okay. I'll send my team as backup.
Be careful.

831
00:44:34,193 --> 00:44:35,194
-Got it.
-Got it.
STYLE
::cue()

832
00:44:37,947 --> 00:44:39,115
[pen clicks]

833
00:44:41,033 --> 00:44:42,118
[pen clicks]

834
00:44:44,078 --> 00:44:45,121
[pen clicks]

835
00:44:46,330 --> 00:44:47,498
[pen clicks]

836
00:44:48,916 --> 00:44:51,627
I should've killed you on that day.

837
00:44:51,711 --> 00:44:52,878
Shut up!

838
00:44:52,962 --> 00:44:54,046
[both grunting]

839
00:44:54,755 --> 00:44:57,091
I'll take away everything you have.

840
00:44:57,174 --> 00:44:58,342
[pen clicks]

841
00:44:58,843 --> 00:44:59,844
[Isoo] Never die.

842
00:45:03,681 --> 00:45:05,474
Live forever, haunted by regret.

843
00:45:06,225 --> 00:45:07,560
-[pen clicks]
-[door opens]

844
00:45:09,603 --> 00:45:10,604
Mr. Choi.

845
00:45:14,317 --> 00:45:15,318
Are you all right?

846
00:45:16,485 --> 00:45:17,486
Not really.

847
00:45:20,698 --> 00:45:23,200
I've been told to find someone
who wants to kill me,

848
00:45:25,244 --> 00:45:26,954
but I can only think of one person

849
00:45:27,580 --> 00:45:29,332
who would want to kill me

850
00:45:30,791 --> 00:45:32,335
and actually be capable of it.

851
00:45:35,087 --> 00:45:36,881
[♪ foreboding music playing]

852
00:45:43,095 --> 00:45:46,766
SPECIAL OPERATIONS UNIT

853
00:46:07,787 --> 00:46:09,997
[♪ foreboding music continues]

854
00:46:41,529 --> 00:46:42,655
[beaker clinks]

855
00:46:51,872 --> 00:46:53,207
Keep quiet and stand by.

856
00:46:56,085 --> 00:46:57,128
[loud knocking]

857
00:46:58,838 --> 00:47:00,047
You have a visitor.

858
00:47:06,554 --> 00:47:07,555
It's your brother,

859
00:47:08,222 --> 00:47:09,223
Jin Isoo.

860
00:47:10,224 --> 00:47:12,476
[♪ gentle melancholy music playing]

861
00:47:59,773 --> 00:48:00,900
[door opens]

862
00:48:02,359 --> 00:48:03,360
[door closes]
STYLE
::cue()

863
00:48:12,495 --> 00:48:13,496
[rattles, clatters]

864
00:48:13,579 --> 00:48:15,206
[♪ foreboding music playing]

865
00:48:16,373 --> 00:48:17,833
Park Gyeongtae, don't move.

866
00:48:24,256 --> 00:48:25,716
Turn around slowly.

867
00:48:37,937 --> 00:48:39,146
Noh Jinsu!

868
00:48:42,733 --> 00:48:43,776
What's all this?

869
00:48:43,859 --> 00:48:45,653
[♪ foreboding music continues]

870
00:49:00,209 --> 00:49:01,210
[gasps]

871
00:49:05,923 --> 00:49:07,967
-Who are you?
-Police.

872
00:49:09,677 --> 00:49:11,720
-[whirring]
-[Gyeongtae] That thing...

873
00:49:11,804 --> 00:49:13,055
It'll blow if we leave it.

874
00:49:16,016 --> 00:49:17,893
-[gun cocks]
-Don't move.

875
00:49:25,943 --> 00:49:27,778
-[dial clicks]
-[whirring stops]

876
00:49:31,031 --> 00:49:32,283
[sniffles]

877
00:49:33,117 --> 00:49:34,201
Is that your next bomb?

878
00:49:35,494 --> 00:49:36,495
No.

879
00:49:38,455 --> 00:49:41,500
It's fertilizer for the future of farming.

880
00:49:41,584 --> 00:49:43,168
Yes, fertilizer.

881
00:49:44,336 --> 00:49:45,921
But it's also used to make bombs.

882
00:49:46,672 --> 00:49:49,008
This is what caused
the explosion in Lebanon.

883
00:49:59,893 --> 00:50:01,103
You made this, didn't you?

884
00:50:05,733 --> 00:50:06,734
[Gyeongtae] Ah...

885
00:50:06,817 --> 00:50:08,360
Ah, that.

886
00:50:08,902 --> 00:50:11,405
It's been all over the Internet
for three years now.

887
00:50:12,323 --> 00:50:14,617
I've already served my time.

888
00:50:14,700 --> 00:50:16,243
I don't do that anymore.

889
00:50:17,536 --> 00:50:19,913
I set it off back then
because of that jerk I worked for.

890
00:50:19,997 --> 00:50:21,123
Lately,

891
00:50:22,541 --> 00:50:24,376
I've been using my brain for other things.

892
00:50:27,838 --> 00:50:29,673
INVENTION COMPETITION

893
00:50:29,757 --> 00:50:31,508
[♪ music swells, fades]

894
00:50:34,845 --> 00:50:35,846
AWARD CERTIFICATE

895
00:50:36,972 --> 00:50:37,973
[Jinsu] A bomb?

896
00:50:38,891 --> 00:50:41,518
[spluttering] It wasn't me.

897
00:50:43,187 --> 00:50:44,396
Then what were you doing?

898
00:50:48,025 --> 00:50:49,234
[exhales deeply]

899
00:50:49,943 --> 00:50:51,195
It's really nothing big.

900
00:50:51,278 --> 00:50:53,614
-You're Jin Isoo's stalker, right?
-Huh?

901
00:50:53,697 --> 00:50:55,616
Were you so obsessed
you wanted to kill him?

902
00:50:55,699 --> 00:50:56,992
We'll talk at the station.

903
00:50:57,785 --> 00:50:59,662
[spluttering]

904
00:51:01,455 --> 00:51:02,456
It's a talisman.

905
00:51:05,376 --> 00:51:06,377
What?

906
00:51:08,379 --> 00:51:09,755
It's a talisman.

907
00:51:11,507 --> 00:51:13,300
People still make bombs like this?

908
00:51:14,176 --> 00:51:15,886
But it'll be tough to catch them.

909
00:51:18,222 --> 00:51:21,433
[chuckles] That's easy to make.

910
00:51:21,517 --> 00:51:24,770
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

911
00:51:27,147 --> 00:51:28,440
The shaman told me

912
00:51:29,858 --> 00:51:32,194
to leave it beside the person
I want to become,

913
00:51:32,277 --> 00:51:34,530
and then I'd receive divine revelation

914
00:51:34,613 --> 00:51:38,200
and make a lot of money like Jin Isoo.

915
00:51:38,283 --> 00:51:40,119
But then it actually blew up.
STYLE
::cue()

916
00:51:41,829 --> 00:51:42,830
Isn't that amazing?

917
00:51:46,291 --> 00:51:47,835
What was inside it?

918
00:51:50,045 --> 00:51:51,046
Well...

919
00:51:51,588 --> 00:51:53,424
My fingernails, some hair,

920
00:51:53,924 --> 00:51:55,050
and the paper talisman.

921
00:51:56,009 --> 00:51:59,513
Then why did your father leave his job?
Wasn't he forced to resign?

922
00:51:59,596 --> 00:52:00,597
My dad?

923
00:52:02,099 --> 00:52:04,268
He moved to the countryside
to take up farming.

924
00:52:05,352 --> 00:52:06,353
He grows persimmons.

925
00:52:15,404 --> 00:52:16,405
It's been a while.

926
00:52:17,531 --> 00:52:18,741
How have you been?

927
00:52:19,324 --> 00:52:21,660
[♪ gentle poignant music playing]

928
00:52:21,744 --> 00:52:23,328
I'm not here to check in on you.

929
00:52:24,955 --> 00:52:25,956
Right.

930
00:52:29,042 --> 00:52:30,461
Someone's trying to kill me.

931
00:52:33,046 --> 00:52:34,047
What?

932
00:52:39,595 --> 00:52:41,805
Someone's trying to kill me with a bomb.

933
00:52:41,889 --> 00:52:43,307
Who?

934
00:52:46,059 --> 00:52:47,060
Yeah.

935
00:52:48,937 --> 00:52:50,147
Who could it be?

936
00:52:51,607 --> 00:52:53,275
No matter how much I think about it,

937
00:52:55,277 --> 00:52:57,154
you're the only one I can think of.

938
00:53:10,959 --> 00:53:12,753
I have a lot of time here.

939
00:53:15,798 --> 00:53:16,799
So...

940
00:53:18,759 --> 00:53:22,179
I keep thinking
about what a fool I've been.

941
00:53:24,640 --> 00:53:25,808
I wrote you a letter.

942
00:53:26,642 --> 00:53:27,726
Several times.

943
00:53:29,770 --> 00:53:30,979
I made excuses

944
00:53:32,648 --> 00:53:34,024
and asked for forgiveness.

945
00:53:35,609 --> 00:53:37,361
But I couldn't bring myself to send it.

946
00:53:39,488 --> 00:53:41,490
Because I don't deserve to be forgiven.

947
00:53:44,409 --> 00:53:45,619
[sighs]

948
00:53:47,412 --> 00:53:48,413
Isoo.

949
00:53:51,375 --> 00:53:52,543
It's not me.

950
00:53:53,418 --> 00:53:55,003
My biggest regret

951
00:53:56,088 --> 00:53:57,214
is hurting you.

952
00:53:57,297 --> 00:53:58,340
Hurting me?

953
00:54:00,008 --> 00:54:01,051
[scoffs]

954
00:54:02,344 --> 00:54:03,345
No.

955
00:54:06,473 --> 00:54:08,559
You ruined my life.

956
00:54:17,985 --> 00:54:19,528
It probably isn't revenge.

957
00:54:24,366 --> 00:54:25,742
The Isoo I know...

958
00:54:28,704 --> 00:54:31,456
would never make someone
want revenge this badly.

959
00:54:32,708 --> 00:54:33,709
It might be...

960
00:54:35,752 --> 00:54:37,212
driven by desire.

961
00:54:44,344 --> 00:54:45,387
[door opens]

962
00:54:46,513 --> 00:54:47,598
[door slams]

963
00:54:48,348 --> 00:54:49,349
Isoo.
STYLE
::cue()

964
00:55:04,865 --> 00:55:06,199
[Mr. Choi] Will you be all right?

965
00:55:06,700 --> 00:55:09,036
I think you should go somewhere safe.

966
00:55:10,287 --> 00:55:11,413
I'll be fine.

967
00:55:11,913 --> 00:55:14,541
This is a police station.

968
00:55:14,625 --> 00:55:16,209
-[chuckles softly]
-[door opens]

969
00:55:20,297 --> 00:55:23,258
Call me if you need anything.

970
00:55:25,969 --> 00:55:26,970
Bye.

971
00:55:31,975 --> 00:55:34,269
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

972
00:55:39,941 --> 00:55:41,777
[♪ pensive music playing]

973
00:55:41,860 --> 00:55:43,362
TARGET BELIEVED TO BE JIN ISOO

974
00:55:44,112 --> 00:55:46,406
I put a surveillance team
on Park Gyeongtae.

975
00:55:46,490 --> 00:55:47,824
We're also tracing his bank accounts.

976
00:55:48,617 --> 00:55:52,496
So anyone can make that kind of bomb,
not just Park Gyeongtae?

977
00:55:53,080 --> 00:55:55,123
Yes. What about the waiter?

978
00:55:56,041 --> 00:55:57,542
He just idolizes Jin Isoo.

979
00:55:58,877 --> 00:55:59,878
[sighs]

980
00:56:03,674 --> 00:56:05,133
Where have you been?

981
00:56:06,176 --> 00:56:07,386
I had somewhere to go.

982
00:56:07,469 --> 00:56:08,637
Don't you get it?

983
00:56:10,389 --> 00:56:11,640
Someone's after you.

984
00:56:12,224 --> 00:56:13,642
I know.

985
00:56:16,687 --> 00:56:18,313
That's why I went to see him.

986
00:56:20,190 --> 00:56:22,109
The one person who wants to kill me.

987
00:56:22,776 --> 00:56:23,860
Who?

988
00:56:26,655 --> 00:56:27,656
My brother.

989
00:56:32,077 --> 00:56:33,078
He...

990
00:56:33,704 --> 00:56:35,789
[Hyera] I know. You don't need to explain.

991
00:56:40,669 --> 00:56:41,670
So?

992
00:56:43,130 --> 00:56:44,172
You think it's him?

993
00:56:46,091 --> 00:56:48,093
He's never had any visitors.

994
00:56:48,719 --> 00:56:50,637
He even refused to see his lawyer.

995
00:56:58,812 --> 00:57:01,398
We're still monitoring Park Gyeongtae,

996
00:57:01,481 --> 00:57:03,734
but we're unable to identify
a suspect at this point.

997
00:57:03,817 --> 00:57:05,485
-[sighs]
-For now, I think we should move

998
00:57:05,569 --> 00:57:07,195
Detective Jin to a safe house.

999
00:57:08,488 --> 00:57:10,157
-A safe house?
-Yes.

1000
00:57:11,074 --> 00:57:14,619
We'll take him to one of the safe houses
secured by the Counterterrorism Team.

1001
00:57:14,703 --> 00:57:15,704
Where is it?

1002
00:57:17,414 --> 00:57:19,875
Sorry, sir,
but I can't share that information.

1003
00:57:21,042 --> 00:57:22,127
What?

1004
00:57:22,210 --> 00:57:24,546
There could be someone
in the station with a grudge.

1005
00:57:25,714 --> 00:57:30,886
Are you saying
the culprit could be one of our own?

1006
00:57:30,969 --> 00:57:32,721
-Sir.
-[Hyera] It's just a precaution.

1007
00:57:34,097 --> 00:57:35,390
Just to be safe.

1008
00:57:35,891 --> 00:57:36,933
[exhales in disbelief]

1009
00:57:37,017 --> 00:57:39,519
All this trouble
just because of one rich kid.

1010
00:57:40,312 --> 00:57:42,898
Safe house or wherever,
just get him out of here.

1011
00:57:42,981 --> 00:57:44,941
-Before something goes wrong.
-Yes, sir.

1012
00:57:45,025 --> 00:57:47,694
Put Team 1 with him. You can trust them.

1013
00:57:48,403 --> 00:57:49,654
Yes, I'll do that.

1014
00:57:54,159 --> 00:57:56,745
Detective Jin Isoo,
you'll be moving to a safe house.

1015
00:57:56,828 --> 00:57:59,372
We're leaving now. Quietly.
Team 1 will join you.

1016
00:57:59,456 --> 00:58:01,082
Where exactly are we going?

1017
00:58:01,666 --> 00:58:02,959
I'll tell you on the way.

1018
00:58:03,043 --> 00:58:04,294
Give me a break.

1019
00:58:04,377 --> 00:58:06,713
I just need to stay holed up at home.
I'm not going.

1020
00:58:06,797 --> 00:58:09,633
We don't have a suspect,
and your place isn't safe either.

1021
00:58:10,217 --> 00:58:12,010
You're a target now.
You don't get to decide.

1022
00:58:15,305 --> 00:58:16,473
[sighs wearily]

1023
00:58:20,602 --> 00:58:21,603
[car alarm chirps]

1024
00:58:21,686 --> 00:58:22,771
Get in this one.

1025
00:58:23,271 --> 00:58:25,357
I can't just ride in any car. [scoffs]

1026
00:58:28,443 --> 00:58:31,071
You want to make it obvious
Jin Isoo is in that car?
STYLE
::cue()

1027
00:58:34,658 --> 00:58:35,659
Get in.

1028
00:58:37,494 --> 00:58:39,496
[muttering] Who does she think she is,
my boss?

1029
00:58:39,579 --> 00:58:40,789
Get in.

1030
00:59:04,020 --> 00:59:06,064
[♪ ominous music plays]

1031
00:59:13,363 --> 00:59:15,240
[Kyungjin] Maybe I should've gotten
in that car.

1032
00:59:15,323 --> 00:59:17,325
I don't think we should leave them alone.

1033
00:59:17,409 --> 00:59:19,411
I'm sure they won't fight.

1034
00:59:19,494 --> 00:59:20,745
They're not kids.

1035
00:59:23,498 --> 00:59:24,875
Nutjob, you asleep?

1036
00:59:28,211 --> 00:59:30,255
What do you want now?

1037
00:59:31,631 --> 00:59:32,716
There's no need to be scared.

1038
00:59:33,300 --> 00:59:34,551
Nothing bad will happen.

1039
00:59:35,302 --> 00:59:36,970
We'll catch them while you're there.

1040
00:59:37,053 --> 00:59:39,264
You think I'm an idiot or something?

1041
00:59:39,347 --> 00:59:40,348
I'm a cop too.

1042
00:59:41,683 --> 00:59:42,684
[chuckles softly]

1043
00:59:45,395 --> 00:59:47,063
Why are you even a cop?

1044
00:59:48,356 --> 00:59:49,733
Picking a fight with me again?

1045
00:59:49,816 --> 00:59:51,443
No, I'm just curious.

1046
00:59:51,526 --> 00:59:53,695
You're incredibly rich,

1047
00:59:53,778 --> 00:59:55,280
and you can do whatever you want.

1048
00:59:56,573 --> 00:59:57,866
Then what about you?

1049
00:59:57,949 --> 00:59:59,910
If you were incredibly rich,
would you quit?

1050
01:00:00,869 --> 01:00:02,704
-No.
-Same with me.

1051
01:00:02,787 --> 01:00:05,749
I've tried and done it all,
but this is my calling.

1052
01:00:06,666 --> 01:00:07,667
What?

1053
01:00:08,209 --> 01:00:09,669
Run out of fights to pick?

1054
01:00:12,714 --> 01:00:13,715
[scoffs]

1055
01:00:14,049 --> 01:00:15,425
You sure are different.

1056
01:00:16,801 --> 01:00:19,137
Says the person
who's been calling me a nutjob.

1057
01:00:19,220 --> 01:00:20,388
[vibrating]

1058
01:00:20,472 --> 01:00:21,556
Just answer your phone.

1059
01:00:24,184 --> 01:00:25,268
It's not me.

1060
01:00:26,269 --> 01:00:27,896
[vibrating continues]

1061
01:00:29,356 --> 01:00:30,357
It's not me either.

1062
01:00:33,276 --> 01:00:34,277
What's that?

1063
01:00:35,779 --> 01:00:38,156
It's a box I've never seen before.

1064
01:00:40,408 --> 01:00:41,993
What are you doing?

1065
01:00:42,869 --> 01:00:44,329
That red light on the box...

1066
01:00:44,412 --> 01:00:45,956
[vibrating continues]

1067
01:00:52,796 --> 01:00:54,047
[♪ ominous music playing]

1068
01:00:54,130 --> 01:00:55,590
[timer beeping]

1069
01:00:56,216 --> 01:00:57,801
-It's a bomb.
-What?

1070
01:00:58,385 --> 01:00:59,844
It's a bomb!

1071
01:01:00,762 --> 01:01:02,472
[tires screeching]

1072
01:01:02,555 --> 01:01:04,641
[♪ tense music playing]

1073
01:01:04,724 --> 01:01:06,726
[car horns blaring]

1074
01:01:15,360 --> 01:01:16,403
What's going on?

1075
01:01:16,486 --> 01:01:17,654
There's a bomb in the car.

1076
01:01:17,737 --> 01:01:19,739
Blast radius is 50... No, 100 meters.

1077
01:01:20,573 --> 01:01:21,700
Take the wheel.

1078
01:01:22,409 --> 01:01:24,119
[inhales sharply, mutters indistinctly]

1079
01:01:32,168 --> 01:01:33,670
[tires screeching]

1080
01:01:36,589 --> 01:01:37,924
Four minutes left.

1081
01:01:44,389 --> 01:01:45,598
[tires screech]

1082
01:01:47,976 --> 01:01:49,102
[exhales sharply]

1083
01:01:50,478 --> 01:01:51,813
-[timer beeping]
-[Isoo mutters indistinctly]

1084
01:01:53,898 --> 01:01:55,316
[engine revving]

1085
01:01:56,234 --> 01:01:57,235
GANGHA QUAY

1086
01:01:58,069 --> 01:01:59,404
I know a place.

1087
01:02:02,198 --> 01:02:03,366
[tires screeching]

1088
01:02:06,661 --> 01:02:07,954
-[car horn blares]
-[tires screech]
STYLE
::cue()

1089
01:02:10,790 --> 01:02:12,459
Wait, stop!

1090
01:02:12,542 --> 01:02:14,544
-[car horn honking]
-[siren blaring]

1091
01:02:20,675 --> 01:02:21,885
[tires screeching]

1092
01:02:34,189 --> 01:02:35,899
[♪ tense music playing]

1093
01:02:42,072 --> 01:02:43,406
[grunting]

1094
01:02:47,660 --> 01:02:48,661
[grunts]

1095
01:02:51,456 --> 01:02:53,041
[Hyera] There are people here. Be careful.

1096
01:02:55,001 --> 01:02:56,461
[car horn honking]

1097
01:02:58,296 --> 01:02:59,380
[grunts]

1098
01:03:00,632 --> 01:03:01,883
[car horn honking]

1099
01:03:05,220 --> 01:03:06,679
[tires screeching]

1100
01:03:07,388 --> 01:03:08,681
Detective Park, stop!

1101
01:03:08,765 --> 01:03:09,766
[tires screech]

1102
01:03:09,849 --> 01:03:11,976
[siren blaring distantly]

1103
01:03:24,322 --> 01:03:25,406
[tires screech]

1104
01:03:28,493 --> 01:03:30,245
-Nine seconds.
-Open the door.

1105
01:03:31,121 --> 01:03:32,539
-What?
-Open the door!

1106
01:03:42,340 --> 01:03:43,675
[suspenseful music intensifies]

1107
01:03:55,395 --> 01:03:56,729
FLEX X COP 2
EPISODE 1

1108
01:03:56,813 --> 01:03:58,022
SERIAL BOMBING ATTACKS BEGIN...
WHO IS AFTER JIN ISOO?

1109
01:03:58,106 --> 01:04:01,526
[♪ upbeat pop music playing,
Hersh "Shadows In The Night"]

1110
01:04:22,630 --> 01:04:26,050
Special Cast.
Kwak Siyang, Kwaktube, Bae Seongjae

1111
01:04:33,141 --> 01:04:34,559
-[cell phone vibrates]
-[distorted voice] Come alone.

1112
01:04:34,642 --> 01:04:36,519
He'll blow up if I see anyone else.

1113
01:04:36,603 --> 01:04:38,396
-[Isoo] Mr. Choi!
-[Hyeonwoo] I got a DM.

1114
01:04:38,479 --> 01:04:40,899
-I was told to come here and film you die.
-Detective!

1115
01:04:40,982 --> 01:04:43,276
-[Hyera] I think Jin Isoo has been set up.
-[explosion]

1116
01:04:43,359 --> 01:04:45,195
I don't know how far ahead they planned.

1117
01:04:45,278 --> 01:04:47,822
Whose idea was it
to do a feature on Detective Jin Isoo?

1118
01:04:47,906 --> 01:04:49,324
[in English] Action.

1119
01:04:49,407 --> 01:04:51,409
[Isoo, in Korean] I think I know
what the bombers are after.

1120
01:04:51,492 --> 01:04:53,578
-[Kyungjin] Isoo disappeared.
-Detective Jin!

1121
01:04:53,661 --> 01:04:54,662
We need a different location.

1122
01:04:54,746 --> 01:04:56,873
-Is this Joo Hyera's place?
-The bomber would never expect it.

1123
01:04:56,956 --> 01:04:59,250
I didn't expect it either.
I'm going to a hotel.

1124
01:04:59,334 --> 01:05:00,335
Once Jin Isoo leaves,

1125
01:05:00,418 --> 01:05:02,295
I'd like to pick his replacement.

1126
01:05:02,378 --> 01:05:03,922
[Isoo] No way. Is someone...

1127
01:05:04,005 --> 01:05:07,050
[Hyera] It sent Jin Isoo to a safe house
and isolated him.

1128
01:05:07,800 --> 01:05:09,677
[Isoo] That bastard was bluffing.

1129
01:05:11,804 --> 01:05:13,556
[narrator, on TV] Next week's Specialist

1130
01:05:13,640 --> 01:05:17,352
is a third-generation billionaire heir
and violent crimes detective,

1131
01:05:17,435 --> 01:05:18,978
Senior Inspector Jin Isoo.

1132
01:05:19,062 --> 01:05:22,607
He recently arrested members
of a pyramid scheme ring in Mexico.

1133
01:05:23,107 --> 01:05:26,527
Detective Jin joined the police through
a special recruitment program for lawyers

1134
01:05:26,611 --> 01:05:29,614
-and has since built an impressive career.
-[sighs] That nutjob.

1135
01:05:29,697 --> 01:05:33,451
Don't miss next week's episode
on Flex Cop Senior Inspector Jin Isoo.

1136
01:05:38,957 --> 01:05:40,959
Translated by Hyesoo Lee

